+V64.3.22 EAF-ICER-TCR engineering validation
+=============================================
+
+Scope
+-----
+Uploaded basis: V64.3.21 EAF-ICER-MCR code + double-fresh screen.
+V22 changes only the post-EAF reliability/operator layer and diagnostics/launcher.
+Frozen: planner-interface evidence cap B<=16, M=24 acquisition, selected evidence,
+EAF value checkpoint/arithmetic, V19/V20 anchor-support and dominance heads,
+final evidence/one-sided certificate, safety mask, and structural-risk guard.
+
+V21 causal findings encoded into V22
+------------------------------------
+1. Split A: incumbent->anchor path -19.85k regret, direct alternative path +143.72k.
+2. Split B: incumbent->anchor path +99.34k, profile-mean alternative path +4.65k.
+3. V21 consensus: higher binary precision can worsen direct path regret (+108.07k on B).
+4. V21 TRAIN retention holdout already had harmful predicted-fallback teacher-margin sums.
+5. Repeated transition 1->4 exists in TRAIN (78 admissible examples; 28.2% teacher-positive;
+   aggregate candidate-minus-incumbent teacher improvement -66.82).
+
+Implemented V22 safety/causal contracts
+---------------------------------------
+- runtime-only planner transition features; no teacher/future input, no raw slot blacklist;
+- TRAIN-only magnitude-weighted regret-risk heads, fixed L2=1e-3 and semantic zero boundary;
+- replacement-risk TRAIN population is frozen support-positive + scalar-dominance-positive;
+- scalar and signed-profile arms share identical risk TRAIN population and risk head;
+- signed profile is ranking-only: scalar dominance fixes binary replacement eligibility;
+- all-flagged structural delegation remains unchanged;
+- deterministic TRAIN fail-close requires non-harmful retention and replacement path sums;
+- A/B fresh blocks must each pass independently; no pooled rescue;
+- 4700 inspected validation tokens are permanently excluded.
+
+Regression / syntax
+-------------------
+V64.3.6--V64.3.22 targeted regression: 108/108 PASS (6 existing warnings).
+Full repository: 396/396 PASS (36 existing warnings).
+V22-specific tests: 7/7 PASS.
+Modified Python modules: py_compile PASS.
+RUN_V64_3_22_EAF_ICER_TCR_SCREEN_2GPU.sh: bash -n PASS.
+Warnings remain the existing PyTorch Transformer nested_tensor/norm_first class.
+
+Backward compatibility
+----------------------
+A prior 5000-case randomized frozen-V21 behavior replay with the V22 regret-risk path
+disabled produced 0 action/score/diagnostic differences and identical SHA256:
+deeccec7da545d50890c3cb611a6f4f3da8b113edd469dff73f11d300f6ef5bf
+The final scalar-positive/profile-ranking policy is only reachable from new V22 configs;
+frozen V21/V20 configs retain their original dominance_policy and behavior.
+
+Leakage audit
+-------------
+Runtime tournament transition/risk path consumes only frozen EAF/frontier diagnostics,
+selected-evidence-derived features, candidate trajectories, maneuver IDs, safety/final-guard
+runtime state, and fitted weights. Teacher margin is used only by the TRAIN-only fitter and
+evaluation diagnostics. Fresh token selection uses scenario identity + fixed SHA256 only.
+No validation/test teacher label enters the fitted config.
+
+Known intentional cost
+----------------------
+V22 requires one new 3000-scene TRAIN replay because old frozen TRAIN edge artifacts did not
+store the candidate transition geometry needed by TCR. This is a one-time frozen TRAIN
+instrumentation cost, not representation retraining. Fresh screen remains paired and uses
+pre-deserialization token filtering.
+
+Status
+------
+Engineering validation PASS. Screen remains a causal screen only. Do not run full/test/
+closed-loop unless both independent fresh blocks pass and the checker explicitly authorizes
+one frozen full-validation reproduction.
+
+Synthetic end-to-end fitter/contract smoke
+------------------------------------------
+A deterministic synthetic TRAIN frontier with 2000 scenes and both positive/negative
+retention/replacement outcomes was passed through the real V22 fitter after the final
+scalar-eligibility/profile-ranking ablation cleanup.
